{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/426893-if-you-were-picking-pantheons-for-a-space-opera","id":426893,"title":"If you were picking pantheons for a Space Opera?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-03T13:04:52-08:00","id":426893,"title":"If you were picking pantheons for a Space Opera?","content":"Basically, if you had a Space Opera setting were the Gods can reconect with humanity out amoung the Stars, which of the Pantheons, that have been written up would you choose? Assume that you get a limit of four.<br /> <br /> Thank-you for your attention.<br /> <br /> Note: Earth is unreachable tech is high, and interplanetary travel is cheap, interstellar is rare and expensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T21:14:20-08:00","id":427363,"title":"","content":"The game &quot;Hellas&quot; does a great job selling Greek myth as perefect inspiration for classically PULPY space-opera.<br /> <br /> On the other end from that kind of a seat of your pants individual action-adventuring - the Celestial Bureaucracy would do well for a more Star Trek/the Culture (we'll uplift you into our peaceful better society) model story.*<br /> <br /> *Yes I know that contradicts the Prime Directive in Stark Trek, I just meant the type of harmonious advanced society the protagonists represent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T21:16:29-08:00","id":427368,"title":"","content":"And of course much has been written on the scifi seeming elements in the Vedas one can draw on with the Deva.<br /> <br /> If you're picking and choosing I'd steer a bit away from the Psedjet and Atzlanti as Ancient Astronauts, just because that feels really played to me, and was a bit steeped in &quot;Brown people couldn't have built THIS!&quot; cultural condescension to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T08:49:09-08:00","id":427760,"title":"","content":"A lot of inspiration out there. <br /> <br /> It's not like original Star Trek didn't do Greek gods. Dr Who did some riffs on Egyptian myths. Patricia Kennealy Morrison did a series (or two?) of space borne Celtic mythology. I didn't like it very much, but she kept getting book contracts. <br /> <br /> I think you could spin the Egyptian and Aztec and not go too Ancient Astronauts on it. I remember some sci fi back when I was kid in a solar system where the planets were named for the Egyptian gods and the story was wrapped around some of the stories. I wish I could remember who wrote it. It was VERY long ago and the patina of years has fallen across it. <br /> <br /> There's ALWAYS Zelazny's Lord of Light. Among other other sci-fi books that feature gods or beings who have taken on godhood. <br /> <br /> I don't think there is a pantheon that can't be taken into space in a compelling way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T09:03:44-08:00","id":427774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/426893-if-you-were-picking-pantheons-for-a-space-opera?p=427760#post427760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think there is a pantheon that can't be taken into space in a compelling way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Loas would be an odd mix. I'm sure something interesting can be done with this combination, but they're the one that strikes me as the oddest.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T11:51:00-08:00","id":427940,"title":"","content":"Loas in space sounds awesome. If someone hasn't written that book already, they need to. <br /> <br /> (I've played in a Con game where the Loa were mapped onto the characters in the Chronicles of Amber and it was one of the most amazing role-playing experiences I have ever had... The Loa are nigh infinitely flexible.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T15:02:56-08:00","id":428200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/426893-if-you-were-picking-pantheons-for-a-space-opera?p=427774#post427774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Loas would be an odd mix. I'm sure something interesting can be done with this combination, but they're the one that strikes me as the oddest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering the Loa are ALL ABOUT displaced population in a new world, not to mention rage against imperialism (a common theme in space opera), seems like it fits pretty well to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T22:55:11-08:00","id":431079,"title":"","content":"I'd have to say the Aesir because there are far, far too many reasons it would fit perfectly!<br /> <br /> 1 - Think of the Heavy Metal videos!<br /> <br /> 2 - A lot of Norse mythology seems related to space, stars and outer realm stuff. Such as the Rainbow Bridge, or the northern lights for instance<br /> <br /> 3 - If Fenrir is big enough to swallow the sun, chances are you're not going to be fighting him on the planet's surface.<br /> <br /> 4 - Space vikings... just imagine a bunch of Scions flying around through space with battle axes and war hammers, smashing the crap out of aliens. Oh, and they'd have FTL motorcycles!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-07-2015, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T16:27:34-08:00","id":431967,"title":"","content":"I would scrutinize heavily on Palladium's Rifts.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/51hfWSob4OL._SY344_BO1,204,203,200_.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T06:33:56-07:00","id":433883,"title":"","content":"Aztec/Mayan gods. One was even said to have come from the stars and returned to them after revealing himself to the mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T07:10:05-07:00","id":433943,"title":"","content":"Plus, the Aztec gods have all this whole feud against the Tzitzimitls (I might have butchered the spelling).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T03:54:11-07:00","id":436886,"title":"","content":"Definitely the Vikings. They are all about melodrama. They were sailors and pirates, something that suits the ideal of travel between planets and maybe finding new things, if not they can be smugglers with ease. At home individual heroes were well known throwing themselves all in and going against whole armies but also being sneaky.Viking heroes also love melodrama, they eat it for breakfast, Lunch, and Dinner. I mean Brynhilda is a figure of Opera for a reason almost seems wrong to leave them out.<br /> <br /> My next bet would be the Yazata due to all the adventures and Good vs Evil that they nail so well. They also love stars. If not Greeks, they have all the family drama of every myth ever, also adventurous and also pretty well known by any group.<br /> <br /> China would be better for a lighter side. I mean it is all built up. Journey to the West could be made into a space opera. You have this government like a federation (Celestial Bureaucracy is almost how starfleet might describe themselves lol), you have trouble makers who we cheer for as they steal everything and good hearted marauders. You have prisoners traveling around doing good deeds to shave time off a long sentence, I mean there is a lot to do with it.<br /> <br /> The Force was kinda inspired by Buddhism even while very different from them, as written many are even converts so Celestial Bureacracy and Vikings, preferably against each other (but just a bit the federation is allied with those darn Klingons) and Yazata always being the group that is unaffiliated because they are too busy doing outlandishly cool things for apparently no reason, but also explain and mentor the heroes (the Jedis) any drama you need just milk Viking and Greek mythology for all its worth. (I mean Oedipus invented secretly a family member to the Soap Opera line up, and no one does needlessly star crossed lovers or people dying tragically and then coming back like the Vikings)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5197-kadakithis","name":"kadakithis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:17:10-07:00","id":439489,"title":"","content":"You could do the whole Egyptian Gods = Goa'uld thing from Stargate...though maybe you don't want to do that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}